Description of CMU Components:
Location
Centrica Langage Power Station is a Combined Cycle Gas Turbine (CCGT) electricity generating station located on Eastern Wood Road on the outskirts of Plympton Devon at national grid reference SX 568 558.

Plant
Langage Energy Centre operates 2 Gas Turbines and one Steam Turbine in a combined cycle design comprising:
2 Alstom GT26B2.2 Gas Turbines with electrical generators (19KV);
2 Alstom Heat Recovery Steam Generators (HRSG);
One Steam Turbine with electrical generator (21KV);
One Air Cooled Condenser;
Offsite gas Above Ground Installation (AGI) and 2.6km of gas pipeline owned and operated by Langage Energy Centre;
3 Step up Transformers (19/21KV ? 400KV); and
Connection to the 400KV volt electrical distribution system owned by National Grid though the Gas Insulated Substation.

Metering
Electrical Generation is MVRNd to the BRITGAS trading account. Site Works Power is netted off Total Generation to leave the balance as net export to the National Grid.

CMU is a 32MW 32MWh Lithium Iron Battery Electric Storage System. The BESS is co-located with a solar PV system and shares a grid connection. The solar PV and the BESS will be separately metered, and registered as separate BMUs. The BESS will connect to the grid via the 20/66 kV substation of the Facility, connecting to additional panels on the 33 kV switchgear. The main assets, elements and systems forming the Electricity Storage Facility are: 
16 containers with Lithium Ion battery modules (LFP), containers further including HVAC, fire extinguishing system and controls; 
8 PCS skids, each comprising of 2x 2000 kVA converter, a 4 MVA 0.8/33 kV step up transformer and a 630A 33 kV Ring Main Unit (RMU);

CMU is a 28MW/56MWh Lithium-Ion Battery Electric Storage System. The BESS is co-located with a solar PV system and shares a grid connection. The solar PV and the BESS will be separately metered and registered as separate BMUs. The BESS will connect to the grid via the 20/66 kV substation of the Facility, connecting to additional panels on the 20kV switchgear. The main assets, elements and systems forming the Electricity Storage Facility are: 
28 containers with Lithium Ion battery modules (LFP), containers further including HVAC, fire extinguishing system and controls; 
7 PCS skids, each comprising of 2x 2000 kVA converter, a 4 MVA 0.8/20kV step up transformer and a 630A 20 kV Ring Main Unit (RMU);

The proposed BESS has a capacity of up to 49.9 megawatts (MW)
The proposals are likely to consist of:
? 30No. battery storage cubes
? 14No. inverters;
? 7No. transformers;
? 1No. 33 kilovolt (Kv) operator substation (23m x 7.4m x 4.45m);
? 1No. 33Kv distribution network operator (DNO) substation to facilitate
network connection (8.7m x 5.7m x 3.5m);
? Office accommodation and welfare facilities (12.2m x 2.4m x 2.59m)
